  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Verdict:** `requirements.cli.setup_css` is implemented and tested. I judged this from the supplied excerpts and did not run the tests or read any other files.\n\n**Implementation** (`src/setup.rs`, `run`, marked `{impl}` for this requirement):\n- If `output.html.additional-css` is absent, `run` creates an array that contains only the Habeas stylesheet path.\n- If it is an array, `run` pushes the stylesheet path only when no existing entry already equals it. Existing entries are left alone, and the stylesheet is added at most once.\n- If it is present but not an array, `run` returns `output.html.additional-css must be an array`. This happens before any file is written, so a bad configuration leaves the project untouched.\n- `css_relative` builds the path from the book source directory plus `habeas.css`, joined with `/`.\n- `is_configured` also checks that the stylesheet is listed, so the Symposium hook agrees with what `run` writes.\n\n**Tests** (`tests/setup.rs`):\n- `setup_is_repeatable` starts from a fixture whose `additional-css` is `[\"md/custom.css\"]` and runs setup twice. It asserts that `md/custom.css` is preserved, that `md/habeas.css` is present, and that `md/habeas.css` appears exactly once. This covers preserving entries, adding once, and idempotence.\n- `setup_rejects_invalid_book_configuration` uses `additional-css = \"wrong\"`. It asserts that setup fails and that stderr contains `output.html.additional-css must be an array`.\n- `setup_uses_src_when_book_table_or_source_setting_is_absent` starts with no `additional-css`. It runs setup and then checks that the session-start hook returns `{\"SessionStart\": {}}`, which means the stylesheet was added. This covers the absent case, though only indirectly.\n\n**Remaining gaps:** These are minor and have no FIXME. The absent-key case is checked only through the `is_configured` hook, not by reading `book.toml` directly. There is also no explicit test with the stylesheet already listed before the first run, but the second run in `setup_is_repeatable` exercises that same branch.",
